= Authors =

vtium is a Rust port derived from kmscon and libtsm. Its code is written by
large language models under the review of:
	Aaron Bockelie

kmscon, from which vtium is derived, was written by:
	David Herrmann <dh.herrmann@googlemail.com>
	Ran Benita <ran234@gmail.com>
	Ted Kotz <ted@kotz.us>
	Scott Moreau <oreaus@gmail.com>
	Dave Reisner <dreisner@archlinux.org>
	Matthew Monaco <unknown>
	Detlef Riekenberg <wine.dev@web.de>
	Marcin Slusarz <marcin.slusarz@gmail.com>
	James Buren <ryuo@frugalware.org>
	Zbigniew Jędrzejewski-Szmek <zbyszek@in.waw.pl>
	ysangkok <ysangkok@gmail.com>
	Hoàng Đức Hiếu <github@zahe.me>
	Swift Geek <swiftgeek@gmail.com>
	Aetf <aetf@unlimited-code.works>
	Mirco Müller <macslow@gmail.com>
	Jocelyn Falempe <jfalempe@redhat.com>

libtsm, from which vtium is derived, was written by:
	Aetf <aetf@unlimitedcodeworks.xyz>
	David Herrmann <dh.herrmann@gmail.com>
	Ran Benita <ran234@gmail.com>

